## Class diagram

The class diagram shows the main BookFlow entities and their relationships. It covers manuscript review and versioning, proofprints and feedback, publication as a book, and distributor stock records.

```mermaid
classDiagram
	class Author {
		+string Id
		+string Name
	}
	class Editor {
		+string Id
		+string Name
	}
	class Publisher {
		+string Id
		+string Name
	}
	class Manuscript {
		+string Id
		+string Title
		+ManuscriptStatus Status
		+DateTime SubmittedAt
	}
	class ManuscriptStatus {
		<<enumeration>>
		Submitted
		AssignedForEditing
		AwaitingAuthorResponse
		AwaitingEditorReview
		Approved
	}
	class ManuscriptStatusHistory {
		+string Id
		+ManuscriptStatus Status
		+DateTime ChangedAt
	}
	class ManuscriptVersion {
		+string Id
		+int VersionNumber
		+string BlobUri
		+DateTime CreatedAt
	}
	class Proofprint {
		+string Id
		+string BlobUri
		+DateTime CreatedAt
	}
	class ManuscriptMetadata {
		+string Id
	}
	class ManuscriptHighlight {
		+int StartOffset
		+int EndOffset
		+string OriginalText
		+string EditedText
	}
	class AuthorFeedback {
		+string Id
		+string Comment
		+DateTime SubmittedAt
	}
	class Book {
		+string Id
		+string ISBN
		+string Title
	}
	class Distributor {
		+string Id
		+string Name
	}
	class StockRecord {
		+int AvailableQuantity
		+DateTime UpdatedAt
	}
	class InventoryLedgerEntry {
		+string Id
		+string SourceEventId
		+string EventType
		+int Quantity
		+DateTime RecordedAt
	}

	Author "1" --> "0..*" Manuscript : submits
	Editor "0..1" --> "0..*" Manuscript : reviews
	Manuscript "1" *-- "0..*" ManuscriptStatusHistory : status history
	Manuscript "1" *-- "1" ManuscriptMetadata : metadata
	Manuscript "1" *-- "1..*" ManuscriptVersion : versions
	ManuscriptVersion "1" <-- "0..*" ManuscriptVersion : based on original
	ManuscriptVersion "1" --> "0..*" Proofprint : generated PDF files
	ManuscriptMetadata "1" *-- "0..*" ManuscriptHighlight : stores highlights
	ManuscriptVersion "1" --> "0..*" ManuscriptHighlight : changes in version
	Author "1" --> "0..*" AuthorFeedback : submits
	ManuscriptMetadata "1" *-- "0..*" AuthorFeedback : stores feedback
	ManuscriptVersion "1" --> "0..*" AuthorFeedback : receives response
	Manuscript "1" --> "0..1" Book : approved as
	Publisher "1" --> "0..*" Book : publishes
	Book "1" --> "0..*" StockRecord : availability
	Distributor "1" --> "0..*" StockRecord : reports
	StockRecord "1" *-- "0..*" InventoryLedgerEntry : ledger entries
```

## New manuscript upload workflow

1. The Web App stores the manuscript file in Blob Storage and its metadata in SQL Database.
2. Blob Storage publishes `ManuscriptUploaded` to Event Grid. Event Grid sends the durable work to an Azure Service Bus topic with separate subscriptions for editor assignment and proofprint generation.
3. The editor-assignment service assigns an editor, saves the assignment, and publishes `EditorAssigned`. Event Grid routes this notification through the API frontend, and the editor-notification service emails the assigned editor.
4. The proofprint-generation service submits the manuscript to the PrintOnDemand API, stores the returned PDF in Blob Storage, and saves its URI and manuscript-version link in SQL Database. It then publishes `ProofprintCreated`; the proofprint-notification service emails the editor a link to the stored PDF.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
	Author([Author]) -->|Uploads manuscript| WebApp

	subgraph Azure[Microsoft Azure]
		WebApp[Web App]
		BlobStorage[(Blob Storage)]
		EventGrid{{Event Grid}}
		ServiceBusTopic[(Azure Service Bus topic)]
		EditorAssignmentSubscription[Editor assignment subscription]
		ProofprintSubscription[Proofprint generation subscription]
		EditorAssignmentService[Editor assignment service<br/>Assigns an editor]
		ProofprintService[Proofprint generation service]
		EditorNotificationService[Editor notification service]
		ProofprintNotificationService[Proofprint notification service]
		SqlDatabase[(SQL Database)]

		WebApp -->|Stores manuscript file| BlobStorage
		BlobStorage -->|Manuscript uploaded event| EventGrid
		EventGrid -->|ManuscriptUploaded| ServiceBusTopic
		ServiceBusTopic --> EditorAssignmentSubscription
		ServiceBusTopic --> ProofprintSubscription
		EditorAssignmentSubscription --> EditorAssignmentService
		ProofprintSubscription --> ProofprintService
		EventGrid -->|EditorAssigned notification| ApiFrontend
		EventGrid -->|ProofprintCreated notification| ApiFrontend
		EditorAssignmentService -->|Persists editor assignment| SqlDatabase
		EditorAssignmentService -->|Publishes EditorAssigned event| EventGrid
		ProofprintService -->|Stores generated PDF| BlobStorage
		ProofprintService -->|Persists proofprint Blob URI and version link| SqlDatabase
		ProofprintService -->|Publishes ProofprintCreated after storage| EventGrid
		ProofprintNotificationService -->|Looks up assigned editor and proofprint link| SqlDatabase
		WebApp <-->|Reads and writes manuscript and user metadata| SqlDatabase
	end

	EmailService[Email service]
	Editor([Assigned editor])
	PrintOnDemandAPI[PrintOnDemand API]
	ApiFrontend[Secured API frontend]
	ApiFrontend -->|Forwards notification| EditorNotificationService
	ApiFrontend -->|Forwards proofprint-ready notification| ProofprintNotificationService
	EditorNotificationService -->|Sends editor assignment email| EmailService
	ProofprintNotificationService -->|Sends email with proofprint link| EmailService
	EmailService -->|Delivers notification| Editor
	EmailService -->|Delivers proofprint-ready notification| Editor
	ProofprintService -->|Submits manuscript for proofprint generation| PrintOnDemandAPI
	PrintOnDemandAPI -->|Returns generated PDF| ProofprintService
```

## Manuscript proofreading workflow

1. The editor highlights and edits the manuscript in the Web App. The app stores the edited file as a new Blob Storage version and saves the highlights and version metadata in SQL Database, then publishes `ManuscriptEdited`.
2. Event Grid sends the proofprint-generation job through Service Bus. The proofprint service submits the edited version to the PrintOnDemand API, stores the returned PDF in Blob Storage, and saves its URI and version link in SQL Database. It publishes `ProofprintCreated` after storage completes.
3. Event Grid forwards the lightweight author notification through the API frontend. The author receives a Web App link, reviews the edits, and uploads a revised version with feedback. The Web App stores the new version and metadata, then publishes `ManuscriptRevised`.
4. Event Grid sends the new proofprint job through Service Bus and forwards the editor notification through the API frontend. The proofprint service stores the author's proofprint PDF and its version link; the editor receives links to the revised manuscript and proofprint.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
	Editor([Editor]) -->|Reviews and highlights manuscript| WebApp

	subgraph Azure[Microsoft Azure]
		WebApp[Web App]
		BlobStorage[(Blob Storage)]
		SqlDatabase[(SQL Database)]
		EventGrid{{Event Grid}}
		ServiceBus[(Azure Service Bus)]
		AuthorNotificationService[Author notification service]
		EditorNotificationService[Editor notification service]
		ProofprintService[Proofprint generation service]

		WebApp -->|Loads original manuscript| BlobStorage
		WebApp -->|Stores edited version linked to original| BlobStorage
		WebApp -->|Stores highlights and version metadata| SqlDatabase
		WebApp -->|Publishes ManuscriptEdited event| EventGrid
		EventGrid -->|ManuscriptEdited proofprint work| ServiceBus
		ServiceBus -->|ManuscriptEdited| ProofprintService
		EventGrid -->|Author notification| ApiFrontend
		ApiFrontend -->|Forwards to author notification service| AuthorNotificationService
		AuthorNotificationService -->|Looks up author and updated-version link| SqlDatabase
		WebApp -->|Stores author feedback and revised-version metadata| SqlDatabase
		WebApp -->|Stores revised version linked to editor's version| BlobStorage
		WebApp -->|Publishes ManuscriptRevised event| EventGrid
		EventGrid -->|ManuscriptRevised proofprint work| ServiceBus
		ServiceBus -->|ManuscriptRevised| ProofprintService
		EventGrid -->|Editor and proofprint-ready notifications| ApiFrontend
		ApiFrontend -->|Forwards to editor notification service| EditorNotificationService
		EditorNotificationService -->|Looks up editor and revised-version link| SqlDatabase
		ProofprintService -->|Stores generated PDFs| BlobStorage
		ProofprintService -->|Persists proofprint URIs and version links| SqlDatabase
		ProofprintService -->|Publishes ProofprintCreated after storage| EventGrid
	end

	EmailService[Email service]
	PrintOnDemandAPI[PrintOnDemand API]
	ApiFrontend[Secured API frontend]
	Author([Author])
	Editor([Editor])
	AuthorNotificationService -->|Sends email with Web App link| EmailService
	EmailService -->|Delivers edited-manuscript notification| Author
	Author -->|Opens updated manuscript link| WebApp
	Author -->|Responds to edits and uploads revision| WebApp
	EditorNotificationService -->|Sends email with revised-manuscript link| EmailService
	EmailService -->|Delivers revision notification| Editor
	EditorNotificationService -->|Sends email with proofprint link| EmailService
	EmailService -->|Delivers proofprint-ready notification| Editor
	ProofprintService -->|Generates proofprint for edited or revised version| PrintOnDemandAPI
	PrintOnDemandAPI -->|Returns generated PDF| ProofprintService
```

## Manuscript and publication progress tracking

Lifecycle events track a manuscript from submission through editing, author feedback, editor review, and approval. Event Grid routes `ManuscriptUploaded`, `EditorAssigned`, `ManuscriptEdited`, `ManuscriptRevised`, and `ManuscriptApproved` through Service Bus to the progress-tracking service. The service updates the current status and history in SQL Database; the Web App displays that progress to publishers and other authorized users.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
	Publisher([Publisher]) -->|Views project progress| WebApp

	subgraph Azure[Microsoft Azure]
		BlobStorage[(Blob Storage)]
		WebApp[Web App]
		EditorAssignmentService[Editor assignment service]
		EventGrid{{Event Grid}}
		ServiceBus[(Azure Service Bus)]
		ProgressTrackingService[Publication progress service]
		SqlDatabase[(SQL Database)]

		BlobStorage -->|ManuscriptUploaded| EventGrid
		EditorAssignmentService -->|EditorAssigned| EventGrid
		WebApp -->|ManuscriptEdited, ManuscriptRevised, ManuscriptApproved| EventGrid
		EventGrid -->|ManuscriptUploaded, EditorAssigned, ManuscriptEdited, ManuscriptRevised, ManuscriptApproved| ServiceBus
		ServiceBus -->|Consumes lifecycle events| ProgressTrackingService
		ProgressTrackingService -->|Updates current status and history| SqlDatabase
		WebApp <-->|Reads manuscript status and history| SqlDatabase
	end
```

## Manuscript approval workflow

When the editor approves a manuscript, the Web App saves the approval status and publishes `ManuscriptApproved` to Event Grid. The event triggers three actions:

- Service Bus delivers print-demand work to the print-demand service, which requests printing from the PrintOnDemand API.
- The API frontend routes an approval email to the author.
- The API frontend routes an availability notification to publisher APIs.

The publisher notification means the book is available for ordering, not that it is physically in distributor stock. Delivery and stock updates are tracked separately.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
	Editor([Editor]) -->|Approves manuscript| WebApp

	subgraph Azure[Microsoft Azure]
		WebApp[Web App]
		SqlDatabase[(SQL Database)]
		EventGrid{{Event Grid}}
		ServiceBus[(Azure Service Bus)]
		PrintDemandService[Print demand service]
		AuthorApprovalNotificationService[Author approval notification service]
		PublisherAvailabilityService[Publisher availability service]

		WebApp -->|Stores approval status| SqlDatabase
		WebApp -->|Publishes ManuscriptApproved event| EventGrid
		EventGrid -->|Print-demand work| ServiceBus
		ServiceBus -->|ManuscriptApproved| PrintDemandService
		EventGrid -->|Author and publisher notifications| ApiFrontend
		ApiFrontend -->|Forwards approval notification| AuthorApprovalNotificationService
		ApiFrontend -->|Forwards availability notification| PublisherAvailabilityService
	end

	PrintOnDemandAPI[PrintOnDemand API]
	EmailService[Email service]
	PublisherAPIs[Publisher APIs]
	Author([Author])
	ApiFrontend[Secured API frontend]
	PrintDemandService -->|Requests manuscript printing| PrintOnDemandAPI
	AuthorApprovalNotificationService -->|Sends approval email| EmailService
	EmailService -->|Delivers approval notification| Author
	PublisherAvailabilityService -->|Notifies book is available for ordering| PublisherAPIs
```

## Publisher print order workflow

1. The publisher checks book availability in the Web App and requests a print quantity for a selected distributor.
2. The Web App stores the order and publishes `PrintOrderRequested`. Event Grid routes it through Service Bus to the print-order service, which submits the title and quantity to the PrintOnDemand API.
3. PrintOnDemand and the distributor send delivery and stock callbacks through the API frontend. Event Grid routes these updates through Service Bus to the inventory service, which updates stock data used by the Web App.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
	Publisher([Publisher]) -->|Checks availability and requests print quantity| WebApp

	subgraph Azure[Microsoft Azure]
		WebApp[Web App]
		SqlDatabase[(SQL Database)]
		EventGrid{{Event Grid}}
		ServiceBus[(Azure Service Bus)]
		PrintOrderService[Print order service]
		InventoryService[Inventory service]

		WebApp <-->|Reads book availability| SqlDatabase
		WebApp -->|Stores title, quantity, and distributor| SqlDatabase
		WebApp -->|Publishes PrintOrderRequested event| EventGrid
		EventGrid -->|PrintOrderRequested, BooksDelivered, StockUpdated| ServiceBus
		ServiceBus -->|PrintOrderRequested| PrintOrderService
		ServiceBus -->|BooksDelivered and StockUpdated| InventoryService
		InventoryService -->|Updates stock and availability| SqlDatabase
	end

	PrintOnDemandAPI[PrintOnDemand API]
	Distributor([Distributor])
	ApiFrontend[Secured API frontend]
	PrintOrderService -->|Submits title and quantity to print| PrintOnDemandAPI
	PrintOnDemandAPI -->|Delivers printed books| Distributor
	PrintOnDemandAPI -->|BooksDelivered callback| ApiFrontend
	Distributor -->|StockUpdated callback| ApiFrontend
	ApiFrontend -->|Publishes validated events| EventGrid
```

## Book production and inventory tracking workflow

PrintOnDemand sends `BooksPrinted` callbacks, and distributors send `BooksDistributed`, `BooksSold`, and `StockUpdated` callbacks through the API frontend to Event Grid. Event Grid routes these inventory updates through Service Bus. The inventory service maintains per-title and per-distributor totals and current stock in SQL Database; the Web App reads this data for availability and reporting.

When a distributor confirms a title is in stock and open for sale, it sends `BookAvailableForSale` through the API frontend. Event Grid routes this lightweight notification through the API frontend to the author-notification service, which emails the author a link to the distributor listing.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
	PrintOnDemandAPI[PrintOnDemand API] -->|BooksPrinted callback| ApiFrontend
	Distributor([Distributor]) -->|BooksDistributed, BooksSold, StockUpdated callbacks| ApiFrontend
	Distributor -->|BookAvailableForSale callback| ApiFrontend
	ApiFrontend[Secured API frontend] -->|Publishes validated events| EventGrid

	subgraph Azure[Microsoft Azure]
		EventGrid{{Event Grid}}
		ServiceBus[(Azure Service Bus)]
		InventoryService[Inventory service]
		AuthorAvailabilityService[Author availability notification service]
		SqlDatabase[(SQL Database)]
		WebApp[Web App]

		EventGrid -->|BooksPrinted, BooksDistributed, BooksSold, StockUpdated inventory work| ServiceBus
		ServiceBus -->|BooksPrinted, BooksDistributed, BooksSold, StockUpdated| InventoryService
		EventGrid -->|BookAvailableForSale notification| ApiFrontend
		ApiFrontend -->|Forwards to author notification service| AuthorAvailabilityService
		AuthorAvailabilityService -->|Looks up author and sale link| SqlDatabase
		InventoryService -->|Updates book totals and current stock| SqlDatabase
		WebApp <-->|Reads inventory and sales data| SqlDatabase
	end

	EmailService[Email service]
	Author([Author])
	ApiFrontend[Secured API frontend]
	AuthorAvailabilityService -->|Emails distributor listing link| EmailService
	EmailService -->|Notifies author book is open for sale| Author
```

## Low-stock and reprint decision workflow

When a title reaches 10 books in stock or stock reaches 0, the distributor sends `LowStockAlert` or `StockDepleted` through the API frontend to Event Grid.

- Service Bus routes the durable stock update to the inventory service.
- The API frontend routes a low-stock email to the publisher, who can review availability in the Web App.
- If the publisher approves extra copies, the Web App publishes `PrintOrderRequested`. Service Bus routes it to the print-order service, which sends the request to PrintOnDemand for delivery to the distributor.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
	Distributor([Distributor]) -->|Stock reaches 10 or 0| ApiFrontend
	ApiFrontend[Secured API frontend] -->|Publishes validated event| EventGrid

	subgraph Azure[Microsoft Azure]
		EventGrid{{Event Grid}}
		ServiceBus[(Azure Service Bus)]
		InventoryService[Inventory service]
		PublisherNotificationService[Publisher notification service]
		SqlDatabase[(SQL Database)]
		WebApp[Web App]
		ReprintDecision{Print extra copies?}
		PrintOrderService[Print order service]

		EventGrid -->|LowStockAlert, StockDepleted, BooksDelivered, PrintOrderRequested| ServiceBus
		ServiceBus -->|LowStockAlert, StockDepleted, BooksDelivered| InventoryService
		InventoryService -->|Updates stock and availability| SqlDatabase
		EventGrid -->|Publisher stock notification| ApiFrontend
		ApiFrontend -->|Forwards to publisher notification service| PublisherNotificationService
		PublisherNotificationService -->|Looks up publisher and book details| SqlDatabase
		WebApp <-->|Reads current stock and book details| SqlDatabase
		WebApp --> ReprintDecision
		ReprintDecision -->|Yes: stores print order| SqlDatabase
		ReprintDecision -->|Yes: publishes PrintOrderRequested| EventGrid
		ReprintDecision -->|No: no print order| NoReprint([No reprint])
		ServiceBus -->|PrintOrderRequested| PrintOrderService
	end

	EmailService[Email service]
	Publisher([Publisher])
	PrintOnDemandAPI[PrintOnDemand API]
	ApiFrontend[Secured API frontend]
	PublisherNotificationService -->|Emails Web App link| EmailService
	EmailService -->|Delivers stock alert| Publisher
	Publisher -->|Reviews stock and chooses Yes or No| WebApp
	PrintOrderService -->|Submits title and quantity| PrintOnDemandAPI
	PrintOnDemandAPI -->|Delivers extra copies| Distributor
	PrintOnDemandAPI -->|BooksDelivered callback| ApiFrontend
	ApiFrontend -->|Publishes validated event| EventGrid
```

## Testing strategy

All application code will be covered by unit tests. Each end-to-end workflow will also have integration tests that verify event publication and handling, service interactions, and the resulting persisted state.

## Private Kubernetes deployment and external ingress

BookFlow's containerized .NET services run in a private Kubernetes cluster. Pods are not directly reachable from external systems. External users and integrations connect through a secured API frontend, which authenticates and validates requests, then throttles them with rate limits before publishing accepted events to Event Grid. This throttling is not durable storage; Service Bus provides durable buffering for background work.

Use a Service Bus topic with a separate subscription per consumer when an event must fan out to multiple services. Use a queue for single-consumer work. Lightweight notifications go from Event Grid to the API frontend over HTTPS, then to private notification services without a Service Bus hop.

Configure Event Grid subscriptions with event-type allowlists so only the work each destination needs is delivered. Use these filters for the current workflows:

| Destination | Event types |
| --- | --- |
| Service Bus: editor assignment | `ManuscriptUploaded` |
| Service Bus: proofprint generation | `ManuscriptUploaded`, `ManuscriptEdited`, `ManuscriptRevised` |
| Service Bus: print demand and orders | `ManuscriptApproved`, `PrintOrderRequested` |
| Service Bus: progress tracking | `ManuscriptUploaded`, `EditorAssigned`, `ManuscriptEdited`, `ManuscriptRevised`, `ManuscriptApproved` |
| Service Bus: inventory | `BooksPrinted`, `BooksDelivered`, `BooksDistributed`, `BooksSold`, `StockUpdated`, `LowStockAlert`, `StockDepleted` |
| API frontend: notifications | `EditorAssigned`, `ProofprintCreated`, `ManuscriptEdited`, `ManuscriptRevised`, `ManuscriptApproved`, `BookAvailableForSale`, `LowStockAlert`, `StockDepleted` |

Some domain events intentionally have two destinations for different responsibilities. For example, `ManuscriptApproved` enters Service Bus for print demand and is sent to the API frontend for notifications; the notification service is not also subscribed to the bus. Apply each filter at the Event Grid subscription so notification-only deliveries are not enqueued.

To handle peak load, Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaling (HPA) can increase or decrease service replicas based on CPU, memory, or custom metrics. Event-driven workers can use KEDA with an Azure Service Bus queue or topic subscription to scale based on message backlog. Set replica and resource limits to prevent downstream dependencies from being overwhelmed.

## Azure application and container architecture

The diagram shows the target Azure deployment of the eight production application containers and the resources defined in [`main.bicep`](../infrastructure/main.bicep). Each application is deployed independently inside private AKS. The secured external ingress forwards requests to the `BookFlow.ApiFrontend` container; the ingress and application deployments are configured separately from Bicep.

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    Users["Authors, editors and publishers"]
    Distributors["Distributor APIs"]
    PrintProvider["PrintOnDemand API"]
    EmailProvider["Email provider"]
    PublisherApis["Publisher APIs"]

    subgraph Azure["Microsoft Azure - BookFlow resource group"]
        Entra["Microsoft Entra ID<br/>JWT authentication and SQL administrator group"]
        ACR["Azure Container Registry<br/>Application images"]
        EventGrid["Azure Event Grid custom topic<br/>Work and notification allowlists"]
        WorkloadIdentity["User-assigned workload identity<br/>AKS OIDC federation and Azure RBAC"]
        GridIdentity["User-assigned Event Grid identity<br/>Service Bus delivery and dead-letter access"]

        subgraph VNet["Virtual network"]
            Ingress["Secured HTTPS ingress<br/>Separately configured"]

            subgraph AKS["Private Azure Kubernetes Service - aks subnet"]
                subgraph Apps["bookflow namespace - independent .NET 10 containers"]
                    Frontend["BookFlow.ApiFrontend<br/>JWT validation, throttling, callbacks and proxy"]
                    WebApp["BookFlow.WebApp<br/>Browser client, manuscripts, versions and orders"]
                    Assignment["BookFlow.EditorAssignment<br/>Editor selection"]
                    Proofprint["BookFlow.ProofprintGeneration<br/>Version-linked PDF generation"]
                    Progress["BookFlow.ProgressTracking<br/>Lifecycle history"]
                    Printing["BookFlow.PrintDemandOrders<br/>Initial printing and reprints"]
